ovember 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Illinois law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>A person in actual possession under claim and color of title made in good faith, who continues for 7 successive years and pays all taxes legally assessed, is adjudged legal owner to the extent of the paper title. (735 ILCS 5/13-109; <a href='https://www.ilga.gov/ftp/ILCS/Ch%200735/Act%200005/073500050K13-109.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Persons holding under such possession by purchase, legacy or descent before the 7 years expire may tack on and benefit if they continue possession and tax payment. (735 ILCS 5/13-109; <a href='https://www.ilga.gov/ftp/ILCS/Ch%200735/Act%200005/073500050K13-109.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Illinois?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Illinois houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Illinois Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Illinois house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Illinois attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/illinois-eviction-notice/'>Illinois Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/illinois-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Illinois guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-illinois/'>We buy houses in Illinois</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><p><em>General information for Illinois Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Illinois house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Illinois attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Illinois\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-illinois/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Illinois Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/illinois-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "ra